      {
        "path": "11.b",
        "anchor": {
          "startChar": 155,
          "endChar": 939,
          "quote": "The camera motion detection method is applied to those motion vectors to solve camera motion parameters; the camera motion detection method includes the following equations to respectively solve camera motion parameters of pan, tilt, and zoom: pan 1 = ∑ j = 1 M / 2  ∑ i = 1 N / 2  MVx  ( 2  j , 2  i + 1 )   tilt 1 = ∑ j = 1 M / 2  ∑ i = 1 N / 2  MVy  ( 2  j + 1 , i ) pan 2 = ∑ j = 1 M / 2  ∑ i = 1 N / 2  MVx  ( 2  j , 2  i )   tilt 2 = ∑ j = 1 M / 2  ∑ i = 1 N / 2  MVy  ( 2  j , i ) pan = pan 1 + pan 2   tilt = tilt 1 + tilt 2 zoom =  ∫ ∇ · MV   v =  ∑ j = 1 M / 2  ∑ i = 1 N / 2  ( ( MVx  ( 2  j , 2  i + 1 ) - MVx  ( 2  j , 2  i ) ) +  ( MVy  ( 2  j + 1 , 2  i ) - MVy  ( 2  j , 2  i ) ) ) =  ( pan 1 - pan 2 ) + ( tilt 1 - tilt 2 )"
        },
